   "evidence": "Lines 77-81 and 103-106 have identical RHS (`\u2200 (P : Ideal A) [P.IsMaximal], let B := Localization.subalgebra F P.primeCompl \u2026; \u03c9 \u2208 ((map R R B F).restrictScalars A).range`); the proof body at lines 111-113 adds nothing beyond `hinj`. Mathlib has no such injectivity lemma: grep of `Mathlib/Algebra/Module/LocalizedModule/Basic.lean` shows only `IsLocalizedModule.injective_iff_isRegular` (line 552), and `isTorsionFree`/`isTorsionFree_of_forall_isRegular` (lines 1422, 1438) transport torsion-freeness to the localization rather than giving injectivity.",
   "file": "TauCeti/RingTheory/Kaehler/FractionRing.lean",
   "fix": "Export the injectivity as its own theorem, e.g. `theorem injective_map_fractionRing [Module.IsTorsionFree A \u03a9[A\u2044R]] : Function.Injective (map R R A F) := (IsLocalizedModule.injective_iff_isRegular A\u2070 _).mpr fun s \u21a6 IsSMulRegular.of_ne_zero (nonZeroDivisors.ne_zero s.2)`, and drop the `\u2203!` restatement; a caller gets it in one line from that lemma, `LinearMap.mem_range`, and `mem_range_kaehler_map_fractionRing_iff`.",
   "issue": "`existsUnique_kaehler_preimage_iff` duplicates `mem_range_kaehler_map_fractionRing_iff`: its RHS is the same four lines verbatim, and its proof is `rw [\u2190 mem_range_kaehler_map_fractionRing_iff, LinearMap.mem_range]` plus the unexported `hinj`. The only new fact, `Function.Injective (map R R A F)` from `[Module.IsTorsionFree A \u03a9[A\u2044R]]` (lines 107-110) \u2014 which the module docstring advertises at line 21 \u2014 is not a declaration, so consumers that need the embedding `\u03a9[A\u2044R] \u21aa \u03a9[F\u2044R]` (the stated downstream use) must reprove it.",
   "line": "102"
  }
